What’s left is smaller:

### Edge cases worth a one-line ruling someday
- **Quick while Rooted** — free move vs “cannot voluntarily change position.” Rooted should win; Quick is spent with no move, or can’t be spent. Not written.
- **Anchored + forced move immunity (GROUNDING STANCE) vs effects that end Anchored on move** — already consistent (you never move, so Anchored holds). Fine.
- **GRAPPLE’s sustained Rooted loop** — we defined it in conversation (re-applies to the original target at the start of your turn while you stay Anchored). Confirm that text is what actually went on the card.
- **Off-turn Quick** (SWAY defense, etc.) — you hold it until the end of *your* next turn. Clear from the new Quick ruling; just make sure card text doesn’t reintroduce “on your next turn” as a special case unless intentional (MIRROR STEP).

### Process / pipeline (not rules text)
- Sim still needs Rooted actually enforced and expired if that code hasn’t been updated yet.
- Sealed stays narrative-only until an item-usage hook exists.
- Any remaining “until your next turn” without start/end should get the same pass Berserker’s got.

### Nothing else large is jumping out
Initiative Shift, Collapse floor, Ward/Debuff scope, Armour→Resist order, Deadly/Weak and Resist/Vulnerable cancel, Thorns (melee only), hand-size floor, status-card-as-token cost — those all have coherent written rules.

So: no more silent fantasy-breakers at the same scale as Rooted. What’s left is edge-case polish and keeping the sim honest with the text.

New rule:
“Until your next turn” (no start/end specified) always means the effect fades at the start of your next turn.